brand: Lib Tech
model name: Golden Orca
model year: 2027
AUD price: $1,399.99
availability status: Preorder
estimated availability: May 1, 2026
board type: Freeride-Powder
flex: 6/10
flex description: Mid-flex, balanced blend of flexibility and stiffness
rider level: Intermediate-Advanced
shape: Tapered Directional
camber type: C2x Directional (shortened rocker between feet with lengthened directional camber to tip and tail, more aggressive and stable than regular C2)
width: Standard
mounting pattern: 2x4 Inserts
available sizes: 150cm, 153cm, 155cm, 157cm, 159cm, 161cm, 164cm
sizing note: Volume shifted board, recommend riding 1-3cm shorter than normal
topsheet: Eco Sublimated Poly Topsheet (eco-friendly sublimation, strong and environmentally friendly)
laminate: Tri-Ax/Bi-Ax Fiber with Basalt Alloy, Carbon X
laminate detail - Basalt Alloy: Lightweight, strong, and damp ride
laminate detail - Carbon X: Carbon fiber strands laid at 30° for more torsional response under feet
core: FP - Fire Power Construction Core (60% Aspen, 40% Paulownia with Tri-Ax and Carbon X glass, incredibly light, fast, responsive)
sidewall material: Birch Internal, UHMW Sintered Sidewall (high-impact, exceptional impact resistance, superior resilience, smooth damped ride)
base: Sintered Knife Cut Base (fast sintered material, die-cut to reduce waste)
edge technology: Magne-Traction (seven strategically placed serrations for edge grip in any condition)
tip/tail protection: UHMW Tip/Tail Impact Deflection (replaces edge around nose/tail with UHMW, easy to repair, reduces swing weight)
weight reduction feature: Lightweight Spin Slim (tapered tip and tail for lighter weight and less swing weight)
designer: Travis Rice
related models: Orca, T.Rice Pro
terrain: Freeride, Powder
